			"Message": "chore(Wind): Prune stale generated upstream stubs and bridge shapes\n\nRemove the vast majority of `Source/Effect/Generated/*Upstream.ts` files, `CommandCatalog.ts`, `ServiceCatalog.ts`, and all `*BridgeShapeGenerated.ts` files that were auto-generated from VS Code upstream interface definitions. These stubs accumulated against interface shapes that have since been restructured upstream and no longer reflect current `Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor` definitions.\n\nRetain and update `IAgentHostFileSystemServiceUpstream.ts` to reflect its source path moving from `vs/platform/agentHost/common/agentHostFileSystemService.ts` to `vs/workbench/services/agentHost/common/agentHostFileSystemService.ts`, dropping the stale JSDoc that referenced an in-memory plugin filesystem scheme no longer applicable to the Wind service layer.\n\nThis cleanup reduces the generated code surface area by hundreds of files, keeping only the single upstream stub that is actively referenced by Wind's agent host bridge implementation.",
			"SHA": "395e841a1cf2654e30a1de8d607fcb59c399dfa3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T02:59:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1933,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Remove mock sync sleep from MountainSyncHelper\n\nStrip the `Effect.sleep(10)` used as a simulated sync delay and its \"Mock sync for now\" comment from the `SyncNowEffect` generator. The Mountain, IPC, and Telemetry services are already injected (though currently unused, denoted by underscore-prefixed parameters), and telemetry logging of the sync attempt is in place; the artificial sleep was the last piece of test scaffolding blocking a real sync cycle.\n\nMountain integration — fetching actual state changes — remains gated by the `// DEPENDENCY: Requires Mountain service integration` placeholder and will be wired in a subsequent change.",
			"SHA": "e59db7abc671d88792fc5c89c8e4e54437d491c8"
		}
